    "summary": "High‑energy set with stellar Bertha, The Other One jam and crisp soundboard",
    "blurb": "The show delivers punchy versions of Bertha, Casey Jones and a seamless He's Gone → Other One → Truckin' transition. Jerry’s guitar cuts cleanly while Phil’s bass anchors the improvisations. Soundboard recordings capture most of the night with only minor hiss and occasional drop‑outs.",
    "review": "What unfolds at Oklahoma City Music Hall on November 14, 1972 is a high‑octane snapshot of the early‑'70 Dead in top form. The first set rolls through classics like Bertha, Casey Jones and an inspired China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider pairing with Jerry’s bright, buzzing tone leading the charge. The second set shines brightest when the band launches into a soaring He's Gone that morphs effortlessly into a wild Other One jam before snapping back into Truckin', showcasing Phil’s deep, phat bass and Bob’s rhythmic steadiness. Donna Jean adds a vibrant vocal lift on Box of Rain, while Keith’s keys provide subtle texture throughout. Despite a faint hiss at the start and a few drop‑outs, the Miller soundboard capture remains clear and well balanced, making this night both historically interesting and sonically rewarding.",
